   "final_rule_text": "Manufacturers must report every thermal incident involving overheating, fire, or suspected thermal runaway to the relevant regulator within 24 hours of learning of it, including incidents that caused no injury or property damage. Within 48 hours, they must notify affected customers and, where there is a credible risk to nearby people or property, provide a safety notice to relevant local authorities and people at risk. Reports and notices must state known hazards, immediate precautions, and how to obtain further information. Manufacturers must promptly update reports as material facts become known."
